### What changed and why

**`inventory.py`** — Added `asyncio.Lock` to serialize all stock mutations, plus a new `reserve()` method.

**`checkout.py`** — Changed the flow from `check → charge → decrement` (TOCTOU race leading to overselling + ghost charges) to `reserve → charge → increment-on-fail`:

1. **`reserve()`** atomically checks and decrements stock under the lock — no two coroutines can both see `stock ≥ 1` when only one item remains.
2. If payment fails, **`increment()`** releases the reservation back into stock under the same lock — no ghost charges because a charge only exists alongside a successful reserve.
